  "notes": "This is a complete game with its own rules; change them if your idea differs (or start from the canvas shell instead). The look and wording come from THEME at the top of game.js (colors, what you collect and avoid, title) and the color tokens at the top of style.css, which start neutral on purpose: set them, and the shapes, for what you are making. game.js is organised theme -> constants -> state -> input -> update(dt) -> draw() -> loop: change the rules in update(), the difficulty in spawn(), and add new shapes to drawShape() (star, coin, gem, drop, spike, rock exist). The status line (#status) and window.__game mirror the game state so it can be checked with preview actions such as [\"click #start\", \"wait 1500\"]. Rename anything that still uses the starter's words in index.html.",
